PART 1 — Fresh Server Setup (Ubuntu)
1️⃣ Update system
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
2️⃣ Install required packages
sudo apt install openjdk-17-jdk postgresql postgresql-contrib unzip wget -y
3️⃣ Verify Java (IMPORTANT)
java -version

👉 Must show:

Java 17 ✅
🚀 PART 2 — PostgreSQL Setup (Correct Way)
4️⃣ Open PostgreSQL
sudo -u postgres psql
5️⃣ Run EXACT commands
CREATE DATABASE sonarqube;
CREATE USER sonar WITH ENCRYPTED PASSWORD 'sonar';

ALTER DATABASE sonarqube OWNER TO sonar;
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE sonarqube TO sonar;

\c sonarqube

GRANT ALL ON SCHEMA public TO sonar;
ALTER SCHEMA public OWNER TO sonar;

\q

👉 This step prevents your “permission denied” error

🚀 PART 3 — Install SonarQube
6️⃣ Download
cd /opt
sudo wget https://binaries.sonarsource.com/Distribution/sonarqube/sonarqube-10.5.1.90531.zip
7️⃣ Extract & Rename
sudo unzip sonarqube-*.zip
sudo mv sonarqube-* sonarqube
8️⃣ Create user
sudo adduser --system --no-create-home --group --disabled-login sonar

👉 If exists → ignore

9️⃣ Set permissions
sudo chown -R sonar:sonar /opt/sonarqube
🚀 PART 4 — Configure SonarQube
🔟 Edit config
sudo nano /opt/sonarqube/conf/sonar.properties

Add:

sonar.jdbc.username=sonar
sonar.jdbc.password=sonar
sonar.jdbc.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/sonarqube
🚀 PART 5 — System Tuning (CRITICAL)
1️⃣1️⃣ Edit sysctl
sudo nano /etc/sysctl.conf

Add at bottom:

vm.max_map_count=262144
fs.file-max=65536
1️⃣2️⃣ Apply
sudo sysctl -p

👉 Must NOT show error

🚀 PART 6 — Start SonarQube
1️⃣3️⃣ Start service
cd /opt/sonarqube/bin/linux-x86-64
sudo -u sonar ./sonar.sh start
1️⃣4️⃣ Check status
sudo -u sonar ./sonar.sh status

👉 Should show:

SonarQube is running ✅
🚀 PART 7 — Access SonarQube
1️⃣5️⃣ Open in browser
http://<your-server-ip>:9000
🔐 Default login
Username: admin
Password: admin
🚪 Open port (Azure)

👉 Add inbound rule:

Port: 9000 → Allow
🚀 PART 8 — Jenkins Integration
1️⃣ Install plugins in Jenkins

Install:

SonarQube Scanner Plugin
2️⃣ Generate token in SonarQube

👉 SonarQube → My Account → Security
Create token:

jenkins-token
3️⃣ Add SonarQube in Jenkins

👉 Manage Jenkins → Configure System

Add:

Name: SonarQube
URL:
http://<your-server-ip>:9000
Token → add credential
4️⃣ Add in Jenkinsfile
stage('SonarQube Analysis') {
    steps {
        withSonarQubeEnv('SonarQube') {
            sh '''
            sonar-scanner \
              -Dsonar.projectKey=myapp \
              -Dsonar.sources=. \
              -Dsonar.host.url=http://<your-server-ip>:9000 \
              -Dsonar.login=$SONAR_AUTH_TOKEN
            '''
        }
    }
}
